The proof-of-work function used by Elide is named TowerHash. TowerHash is built
on the Poseidon2b permutation over binary tower fields, published as:

  "Poseidon(2)b: Binary Field Versions of Poseidon/Poseidon2"
  Lorenzo Grassi et al., IACR ePrint 2025/1893
  https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/1893

Elide instantiates that permutation with its own round constants, domain
separation tags, sponge schedule and nonce lane. The permutation itself is
unmodified in structure; Elide does not claim to have designed it.
